    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17925" root="زكم" body-key="z">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَكَّمَهُ</span></b>  is said by Golius to be <i>syn. with</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَزْكَمَهُ</span>. But the only mention of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زكّم</span> that I find
is in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زكن</span> in the S, where it is said that
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زكّن عَلَيْهِ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زكّم</span> signify <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَبَّهَ عَلَيْهِ</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَبَّسَ</span>.]

